  "description": "Reid Let’s Commute | Electric commuter bike\nComfortable, practical and designed for everyday journeys – the Reid Let’s Commute combines electric assistance, commuter-ready features and a relaxed riding position for urban travel.\nThe Reid Let’s Commute is designed to make everyday travel easier, whether you're commuting to work, navigating city streets or running errands. Its 6061 alloy frame features internal cable routing and an integrated 352Wh battery, creating a clean, streamlined design with balanced handling.\nA responsive 250W rear hub motor with 430W peak power provides electric assistance to help you tackle inclines and navigate urban routes, with assistance up to 35km/h. The Ananda D19 handlebar-mounted display features Bluetooth connectivity and app compatibility, keeping essential ride information within easy reach. An L-TWOO 7-speed trigger shifter paired with a Shimano rear derailleur provides practical gearing for changing city terrain.\nTektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors front and rear deliver reliable stopping power and control in varying conditions. Wide 700 x 45c commuter tyres provide added stability and cushioning over potholes and uneven road surfaces, helping create a smoother everyday ride.\nAn oversized 700mm alloy riser bar supports a relaxed, upright riding position, while comfortable rubber grips and a plush city comfort saddle enhance comfort on longer journeys. Finished in a striking turquoise colour, the Let’s Commute combines practical features with a distinctive look for everyday urban cycling.\nThe Let’s Commute is ideal for:\n\nEveryday commuters looking for a comfortable way to travel to work with electric assistance\n\nCity and urban riding, with a practical setup for navigating streets and cycle routes\n\nRiders tackling hills and varied terrain, with a 250W motor delivering up to 430W peak power\n\nRiders seeking higher-speed assistance, with electric assistance up to 35km/h\n\nComfort-focused cyclists, with wide 700 x 45c tyres, rubber grips and a city comfort saddle\n\nConfident urban riding, with Tektro hydraulic disc brakes and 180mm rotors front and rear\n\nRiders who prefer an upright position, with a wide 700mm riser bar for added control\n\nDaily journeys and errands, with an integrated 352Wh battery and a Bluetooth-compatible display\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
